<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The app mark: the progress ring, and nothing else.

    The same arc that carries "today" in the app (core/widgets/progress_ring.dart)
    and on the home-screen widget. One arc at three sizes is what makes the
    three read as one product.

    ## The geometry, and why it's expressed like this

    The spec is a 100x100 canvas: track `circle cx=50 cy=50 r=34` stroked at
    13 in the accent at 22%; arc the same circle stroked at 13 in the accent,
    round cap, `stroke-dasharray: 154 214` — 72% of the 213.6 circumference —
    rotated -90 so it starts at twelve o'clock.

    An adaptive icon's canvas is 108x108dp with only the **middle 66dp**
    guaranteed unclipped by a launcher mask, so the 100x100 artwork is placed
    inside a 108 viewport and scaled to sit within that safe circle. A ring
    that a round mask crops is a ring with a bite out of it.

    `stroke-dasharray` has no vector-drawable equivalent, so the 72% arc is
    drawn as an explicit arc path instead: from 12 o'clock, 259.2° clockwise
    (0.72 x 360), which lands at 169.2° — hence the large-arc flag and the end
    point below.

    Nothing but stroke: no letter, no gradient, no glyph. It has to stay
    legible at 32px, and theming cannot break what has no fill.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <!--
        The 100x100 artwork placed inside the 108 viewport's 66dp safe circle.

        The ring's outer radius is 34 + 13/2 = 40.5. Scaled by 0.80 that is
        32.4, just inside the safe radius of 33 — so no launcher mask, round
        or squircle, can clip it. The translate re-centres the scaled artwork
        on the viewport's own centre (54,54): 54 - 50 x 0.80 = 14.
    -->
    <group
        android:scaleX="0.80"
        android:scaleY="0.80"
        android:translateX="14"
        android:translateY="14">
        <!-- Track: the full circle at 22%, as two half arcs. A single
             near-360 arc leaves a hairline seam where its ends meet. -->
        <path
            android:pathData="M16,50 A34,34 0 1 1 84,50 A34,34 0 1 1 16,50 Z"
            android:strokeColor="#9184D9"
            android:strokeAlpha="0.22"
            android:strokeWidth="13"
            android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent" />
        <!--
            The arc: 72% of the circle, from twelve o'clock, clockwise, round
            cap.

            `stroke-dasharray: 154 214` has no vector-drawable equivalent, so
            the dash is drawn as an explicit arc instead. 0.72 x 360 = 259.2
            degrees from (50,16) lands at (16.60, 56.37); large-arc-flag is 1
            because the sweep exceeds 180, sweep-flag is 1 for clockwise.
        -->
        <path
            android:pathData="M50,16 A34,34 0 1 1 16.60,56.37"
            android:strokeColor="#9184D9"
            android:strokeWidth="13"
            android:strokeLineCap="round"
            android:fillColor="@android:color/transparent" />
    </group>
</vector>
